1.5 cocotb

  Component: cocotb
  Role:      Python coroutine-based testbench framework; driver at
             `lib/services/simulator/cocotb_driver.dart`. SimCrux spawns
             `make SIM=<sim> TOPLEVEL=<top> …` against the user's own
             testbench Makefile, which includes cocotb's installed
             `Makefile.sim` (`cocotb-config --makefiles`), and parses
             cocotb's plain-text stdout summary with regular expressions.
  License:   BSD-3-Clause
  Upstream:  https://github.com/cocotb/cocotb
  Copyright: Potential Ventures Ltd and the cocotb contributors

  **No cocotb Python source is vendored into this repository.** SimCrux
  imports nothing from cocotb, does not drive cocotb's Python runner API,
  and does not invoke pytest. See `docs/cocotb-strategy.md` for why the
  `make`-wrapping approach was chosen over the Python runner. The `.py`
  files under `test/fixtures/projects/` are SimCrux's own test testbenches
  that `import cocotb` exactly the way any end-user testbench would.

  Note that cocotb itself drives one of the simulators above (selected by
  the `SIM=` environment variable, default `icarus`) through VPI/VHPI. That
  linkage is between cocotb and the simulator, inside the child process
  tree — SimCrux is not a party to it.

