8. SQLite (public domain) — the one native library in the graph
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Component: SQLite
Role:      The C library behind the regression trend store. Reached at
           run time through `sqflite_common_ffi` → the `sqlite3` Dart
           package (§7.4), which uses `dart:ffi` to open the SQLite
           shared library.
License:   Public domain
Upstream:  https://www.sqlite.org/

SimCrux does **not** depend on `sqlite3_flutter_libs` and therefore ships
no SQLite binary of its own: the `sqlite3` package opens the host's SQLite
(`libsqlite3.dylib` on macOS, `libsqlite3.so` on Linux — both present by
default). On Windows there is no system SQLite, so a
`sqlite3.dll` must be supplied by the distribution or the environment; that
packaging decision is unresolved. See §9.

SQLite's authors have dedicated the code to the public domain, so no
attribution is legally required. It is recorded here because it is the only
native library SimCrux's dependency graph loads, and because the Windows
packaging question above is a real open item.


